## 2. Testing Portrait and Landscape Orientation

After opening the calculator app, I used the emulator's **Rotate** button to change the screen orientation.

| Orientation              | Observation                                                               |
| ------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Portrait                 | The calculator buttons and display were properly aligned and easy to use. |
| Landscape                | The screen became wider, and the UI adjusted to the available space.      |
| Rotated back to Portrait | The application returned to the normal layout without crashing.           |

### UI Issues Checked

* Buttons overlapping each other
* Text getting cut off
* Incorrect button size
* Empty or unused space
* Screen content not rotating properly

**Observed Result:** No major UI issue was noticed. The layout adjusted correctly when switching between portrait and landscape mode.

**Conclusion:** The application handled screen rotation properly and remained usable in both orientations.

